WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.590
(dramatic music)

00:00:05.168 --> 00:00:08.544
- [Protestors] Deport gays, deport gays,

00:00:08.544 --> 00:00:10.090
God is great, deport gays!

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.040
- [Michael] I'd walk down the
hall and get called “faggot”

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.213
by some folks.

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.704
- [Protestor] Get rid of 'em.

00:00:14.704 --> 00:00:15.861
- [Protestor] Get rid of 'em.

00:00:15.861 --> 00:00:17.310
(cheering)

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.197
- A friend of mine says,
"You know, Michael,

00:00:19.197 --> 00:00:21.067
"you weren't the first
homosexual at P&amp;G

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.797
"but you sure did put a public face

00:00:22.797 --> 00:00:24.444
"to it in the '80s."

00:00:24.444 --> 00:00:27.191
(protestors chanting)

00:00:27.191 --> 00:00:28.424
(dramatic music)

00:00:28.424 --> 00:00:31.600
- [Woman] We will have civil rights

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.420
for gay people.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.067
- Oh boy, Cincinnati in the '80s.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.940
(sighs)

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.690
It was kind of a risky thing,

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.070
being known as gay then.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.180
- [News Announcer] AIDS has struck 1,640--

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.450
- You had a life span of six months,

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.870
maybe 18 months if you were lucky.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.773
There weren't effective remedies then.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.160
- Procter and Gamble
really found this niche

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.157
with Peridex prescription mouthwash

00:00:55.157 --> 00:00:57.950
being used by people with AIDS.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.400
- There was this disconnect.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:00.810
P&amp;G wanted to do the science,

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:01.643
they wanted to do the marketing,

00:01:01.643 --> 00:01:03.520
but they didn't quite get,

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.890
because they weren't gay,

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.883
that these are people's lives.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.320
- Things were not good

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.490
for the LGBT community.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.880
In P&amp;G, the words
“sexual orientation” were

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.100
not in the EEO policy statement.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.290
- You know, where are the gays?

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.180
Where are the lesbians?

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.340
- [Man] The words needed to be there.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.260
- They were not ready to embrace that.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.083
They were not wanting to embrace it.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:32.830
- [Man] In no way was
Michael going to back away.

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:35.013
- I just kept at it.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.210
- He was willing to put it on the line.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.263
- He was willing to be an outlier.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.380
- It's either gonna take you

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.200
or you're gonna take it.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.500
And I had made up my mind.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.180
- Policies do matter.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:55.393
Taking a stand matters.
Words matter.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:01.110
- It's important to
understand the struggle

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.493
because the truth is, we're
always in the struggle.

